    "q-161654": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161654",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find the volume of the solid $R$ given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1-x\\le y\\le 1+x,\\,0\\le z\\le xy\\}.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type I region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-x}^{1+x}{\\int }_{0}^{xy}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-x}^{1+x}[z]_{z=0}^{z=xy}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-x}^{1+x}xy\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=1-x}^{y=1+x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x}{2}((1+x)^{2}-(1-x)^{2})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x}{2}((1+2x+{x}^{2})-(1-2x+{x}^{2}))\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x}{2}(4x)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
