    "q-161660": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161660",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find the volume of the solid $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le 2-{x}^{2},\\,-1\\le y\\le x\\}.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type III region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2-{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{-1}^{x}\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2-{x}^{2}}[y]_{y=-1}^{y=x}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2-{x}^{2}}(x-(-1))\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2-{x}^{2}}x+1\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(x+1){[z]}_{z=0}^{z=2-{x}^{2}}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(x+1)(2-{x}^{2}-0)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}-{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+2x+2\\,dx \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+2x]}_{x=-1}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{3}+1+2)-(-\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{3}+1-2) \\\\  & =2(2-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
